If a clinician conducts a taper then it is possible that the clinician must occasionally pause the taper.
If a clinician conducts a paused-taper for a patient and the patient is ready then it is possible that the clinician must occasionally restart the paused-taper.
If a clinician conducts a taper for a patient and the patient reaches a low-opioid-dosage then it is possible that the clinician must occasionally slow the taper.
